# Docker related files
# Root-relative patterns match only the context root, so a bare `.env` left apps/api/.env,
# apps/api/.env.test, apps/mobile/.env and apps/web-player/.env.development in every build
# context. They never reached a production image — the final stages copy named artifacts rather
# than the tree — but they did land in the `COPY . .` layer of the build stage, which is exported
# to the registry as build cache.
**/.env
**/.env.*
nginx/logs/
backups/

# Dependencies
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
npm-debug.log
yarn-error.log
pnpm-debug.log

# Development
*.log

# Build outputs. Prefixed with **/ for the same reason as the env files above: a root-relative
# pattern matches only the context root, so a bare `.next/` left apps/*/.next and packages/*/dist
# in the context. That shipped a local dev build into the production image and sent gigabytes of
# artifacts to the daemon on every build — apps/ alone is 2.3 GB with them.
**/dist/
**/build/
**/.next/
**/out/
**/coverage/
**/.turbo/
**/test-results/
**/playwright-report/
apps/desktop/src-tauri/target/
graphify-out/

# Keep example file
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.sample
!**/.env.template
